cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or model in your research, please cite this repository and the associated manuscript."

title: "Optimal Stopping Formulation Coupling Entry Tear Diameter, False Lumen Expansion, and Serial Enlargement for Preemptive TEVAR After Type B Dissection"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Prihantini"

    

repository-code: "https://github.com/TitinPrihantini4/tbad-tevar-optimal-stopping-model"

abstract: >-
  This repository contains the computational implementation, model inputs,
  numerical results, figures, and reproducibility materials for a
  literature-informed mathematical proof-of-concept that formulates
  continued surveillance versus preemptive thoracic endovascular aortic
  repair (TEVAR) in uncomplicated type B aortic dissection (TBAD) as a
  state-dependent optimal-stopping problem. The framework combines
  observable aortic morphology with model-defined latent dynamics,
  regime switching, theoretical waiting and procedural intensities,
  and a finite-horizon Bellman decision rule. The model has not been
  calibrated or validated using patient-level longitudinal outcomes,
  and its model-derived stopping boundaries should not be interpreted
  as clinical treatment recommendations.

keywords:
  - type B aortic dissection
  - TBAD
  - TEVAR
  - optimal stopping
  - mathematical modelling
  - dynamical systems
  - Bellman equation
  - ordinary differential equations
  - continuous-time Markov chain
  - sensitivity analysis
  - computational modelling

